# Godot Lab Standards

- Read `AGENTS.md`, the claimed board card, and its work order before editing.
- Keep gameplay state deterministic and save-compatible unless a T3 card says
  otherwise. Do not put authoritative logic only in UI code.
- Keep input, player, world generation, HUD, audio, and save changes separated
  into small commits whenever possible.
- Add or update a focused headless self-test when a behavior is objectively
  testable. Run the project self-test after integration changes.
- For visual work, create a reproducible launch path and record the manual
  check on the board. Do not declare a visual result verified only from code.
- Use existing project conventions and assets before introducing a dependency.

